r-Ashur I</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Puzur-Ashur I was an early ruler of the city of Assur in northern Mesopotamia, around the twentieth century BCE.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/puzur-sin"><span class="enc-name">Puzur-Sin</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Puzur-Sin was a native Assyrian ruler of Assur in the eighteenth century BCE.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/pyatigorsk"><span class="enc-name">Pyatigorsk</span><span class="enc-type">Place</span><span class="enc-snip">Pyatigorsk is a spa town in Stavropol Krai, Russia, in the Caucasian Mineral Waters area at the foot of Mount Beshtau, whose five peaks give the town its name.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/pybba-of-mercia"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/pybba-of-mercia.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Pybba of Mercia</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Pybba was an early king of the Mercians around 600, known only from later royal genealogies.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/pye-min"><span class="enc-name">Pye Min</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Pye Min was king of the Restored Toungoo dynasty of Burma from 1661 to 1672.</span></a></li></ul>
